From 0ba4ef655739dbf5cdb33568766347d7ec30be51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael John <mj@tierone.software>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:33:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sed: do not form a zero offset from NULL in regsub

regsub() started with dst = sp->space + sp->len on a never-used
substitute space (space == NULL, len == 0): a zero offset from NULL is
undefined behaviour (UBSan "applying zero offset to null pointer",
process.c:720), hit by the first substitution of every run and seen
from both fuzz_sedcompile and fuzz_seddata.  Same UB class as the
cspace()/ed/sort zero-length copy fixes; behaviour was correct, UB
only.

Only form space + len for a live buffer (the cspace() len > 0 guard
idiom).  The regsub output paths (&, backrefs, global, zero-width
matches) are pinned by tests in 12-regress-tools.sh, and
fuzz/corpus/sedcompile/regsub-null-dst-ubsan is a minimal reproducer
(matches at pattern-space offset 0 on the harness's first input line,
which is the only path that reaches regsub with a fresh space).

Co-Authored-By: Hermes Agent <hermes@tierone.software>
---
 fuzz/corpus/sedcompile/regsub-null-dst-ubsan | 1 +
 src.freebsd/sed/process.c                    | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 fuzz/corpus/sedcompile/regsub-null-dst-ubsan

diff --git a/fuzz/corpus/sedcompile/regsub-null-dst-ubsan b/fuzz/corpus/sedcompile/regsub-null-dst-ubsan
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..21e1dbda
--- /dev/null
+++ b/fuzz/corpus/sedcompile/regsub-null-dst-ubsan
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+s/h/x&/
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/src.freebsd/sed/process.c b/src.freebsd/sed/process.c
index 3257ba6f..11d5250a 100644
--- a/src.freebsd/sed/process.c
+++ b/src.freebsd/sed/process.c
@@ -717,7 +717,13 @@ regsub(SPACE *sp, char *string, char *src)
 		dst = sp->space + sp->len;				\
 	}
 
-	dst = sp->space + sp->len;
+	/*
+	 * sp->space is still NULL on the first use of a fresh space
+	 * (sp->len == 0); even a zero offset from NULL is UB, so only
+	 * form space + len for a live buffer (same guard idiom as the
+	 * cspace() len > 0 fix).
+	 */
+	dst = sp->len > 0 ? sp->space + sp->len : sp->space;
 	while ((c = *src++) != '\0') {
 		if (c == '&')
 			no = 0;
-- 
